{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CekgdBTQjscDMH88VuCD5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! The implementation is complete and all tests pass. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` endpoint with the following changes:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **Added error code** (`ApiError.kt`):\n   - Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum for when trying to confirm a cancelled shipment\n\n2. **Implemented confirm endpoint** (`ShipmentController.kt`):\n   - Added `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint\n   - Returns 404 if shipment doesn't exist\n   - Returns 409 (Conflict) if shipment is already CANCELLED\n   - Idempotent: returns 200 if already CONFIRMED (succeeds without changes)\n   - Moves CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED status and persists the change\n\n3. **Added comprehensive tests** (`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`):\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment → transitions to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment → succeeds without changes\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment → rejected with 409 and `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment → rejected with 404 and `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` code\n\n### Test Results\n\nAll 17 tests pass:\n- 4 original shipment tests ✅\n- 5 new confirm endpoint tests ✅\n- 4 order tests ✅\n- 3 customer tests ✅\n- 1 application test ✅\n\nThe implementation preserves the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture, requires no new dependencies, and only modifies files within the shipment feature."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":37889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo